---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="OpenCAD Web privacy policy — local-first, no tracking, minimal data.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</p>

  <h2>Your drawings stay on your device</h2>
  <p>
    OpenCAD Web is a local-first application. The CAD engine runs entirely in your browser
    via WebAssembly. The DWG/DXF files you open are parsed on your machine and stored in
    your browser's IndexedDB storage. We have no servers that receive your drawings.
    There is no cloud, no upload, and no account system.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do collect</h2>
  <p>We run <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, a privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics
  service that reports aggregate page views and rough geography. It does not identify individual
  visitors and requires no consent banner.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site displays advertisements served by <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. AdSense uses
    cookies or similar technologies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other
    websites. Google's use of advertising cookies is described in
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's
    Advertising page</a>. You can opt out of personalized advertising at
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads
    Settings</a>. AdSense may collect information such as device type, approximate location, and
    pages visited to decide which ads to show. No ad is ever displayed over the CAD canvas.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    AdSense may place cookies to serve and measure ads. We do not use cookies for our own
    tracking. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The app and site link to external services (GitHub for source code, YouTube for tutorials).
    Those services have their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
